></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zagwe-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zagwe-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Zagwe dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Zagwe dynasty was a ruling dynasty of the northern Ethiopian highlands that rose to power after the decline of Aksum, from around 940 CE according to the chronology.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zahara-de-la-sierra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zahara-de-la-sierra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Zahara de la Sierra</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Zahara de la Sierra is a village in the province of Cádiz, Spain, crowned by a Moorish castle above the Guadalete valley.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/zahir-al-din-marashi"><span class="enc-name">Zahir al-Din Mar'ashi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Zahir al-Din Mar'ashi was a Persian historian of the 15th century from the Mar'ashi family of sayyids who ruled Mazandaran.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zahir-al-umar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zahir-al-umar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Zahir al-Umar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Zahir al-Umar was an Arab sheikh of the Zaydani clan who built an autonomous domain in Galilee in the 18th century, taking Tiberias and making Acre his capital and a…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/al-zahrawi"><span class="enc-name">Al-Zahrawi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Al-Zahrawi, known in Latin as Abulcasis, was a physician of al-Andalus who worked at Córdoba and is regarded as one of the greatest surge