ata.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zaporozhian-cossacks"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zaporozhian-cossacks.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Zaporozhian Cossacks</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Zaporozhian Cossacks were the Cossacks of the lower Dnieper, organised from the 16th century around the fortified Zaporozhian Sich beyond the river's rapids.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zapotec-civilization"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zapotec-civilization.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Zapotec civilization</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Zapotec civilization arose in the Valley of Oaxaca in southern Mexico, where from about 500 BCE Monte Albán became one of the first cities and states of Mesoamerica.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zapotecs"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zapotecs.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Zapotecs</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Zapotecs are an indigenous people of Oaxaca in southern Mexico.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zappo-zap"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zappo-zap.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Zappo Zap</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Zappo Zap were a Songye group from the Kasai region of the Congo, named after their leader Zappo Zap, who settled near Luluabourg in the 1880s and became…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/zara-yaqob"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/zara-yaqob.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" 